window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b190-fc0babacb5cc268d.json"]={sha256:"fc0babacb5cc268dc4e1cd3647f42e648bf1285338614eae6983a436d83f23a8",value:{"id":"b190","title":"砂井與垂直排水板","titleEn":"Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"砂井與預製排水板縮短軟土排水路徑，使超額孔壓較快消散，但不會直接消除土的可壓縮性。本課以網格幾何、等效直徑、水平壓密時間與安裝塗抹為主線，連結井阻、載重、沉陷及排水老化，建立以孔壓與變形共同判斷的卸載交接條件。","summaryEn":"Sand drains and prefabricated drains shorten drainage paths and accelerate excess-pressure dissipation without eliminating compressibility. The course connects grid geometry, equivalent diameter, radial time and installation smear to well resistance, loading, settlement and drain deterioration, establishing unloading and handover criteria from both pressure and movement.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-ground","subcategoryTitle":"地盤改良與地下維護","subcategoryTitleEn":"Ground improvement and underground maintenance","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-ground","learningTags":["underground","ug-ground","ground"],"architectureFamily":"ground","architectureNodes":[["排水距離尺度","Drainage-length scale"],["三角網格影響徑","Triangular-grid influence diameter"],["徑向時間因子","Radial time factor"],["有效應力成長","Effective-stress gain"],["排水能力衰減","Discharge-capacity deterioration"],["壓密度與卸載","Consolidation and unloading"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[3,0]],"diagram":{"type":"ground","labels":["排水距離尺度","三角網格影響徑","徑向時間因子","有效應力成長","排水能力衰減"],"labelsEn":["Drainage-length scale","Triangular-grid influence diameter","Radial time factor","Effective-stress gain","Discharge-capacity deterioration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創教學例：僅作固定無因次幾何與材料參數的擴散尺度比較，長路徑Llong=5 m、短路徑Lshort=1 m，時間比tshort/tlong=(1/5)²=0.0400。若短路徑增加10%至1.1 m，時間比變為(1.1/5)²=0.0484，比原比值增加21%。這不是排水板網格改變後的實際工期比例，因為井徑比、塗抹範圍及井阻可能同步改變。工程設計仍須用完整徑向壓密關係並配合孔壓、沉陷與排水能力觀測，確認各層剩餘壓密而非直接套用平方比。","textEn":"Original teaching example: compare diffusion scales only while holding dimensionless geometry and material parameters fixed. With Llong=5 m and Lshort=1 m, tshort/tlong=(1/5)²=0.0400. Increasing the short length by 10% to 1.1 m changes the ratio to (1.1/5)²=0.0484, a 21% increase in that ratio. This is not the actual schedule ratio after changing a drain grid, because drain-size ratio, smear extent and well resistance may change simultaneously. Engineering design still requires the complete radial-consolidation relationship and observations of pore pressure, settlement and discharge capacity to establish residual consolidation in each layer.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b190-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「排水距離尺度的機理與驗證」與「三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification\" and \"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b190-v14-01","title":"排水距離尺度的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「排水距離尺度」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drainage-length scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"排水路徑縮短會加快壓力擴散，理想擴散時間隨特徵長度平方變化，這是垂直排水構想的基礎。實際排水板網格同時改變影響半徑、井徑比與塗抹比例，不能只用長度平方比直接預測現場工期；土層排水方向也需要辨識。本比值特別保持無因次參數不變，並非排水板間距改變後的工期比；實際n、塗抹與井阻會一同變動。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水距離尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shorter drainage paths accelerate pressure diffusion, whose ideal characteristic time varies with squared length. This motivates vertical drains, but actual spacing changes influence radius, drain-size ratio and smear proportion together. A length-squared ratio alone therefore cannot predict field schedule, and relevant drainage directions must also be identified. This ratio explicitly holds dimensionless parameters fixed and is not the schedule ratio after changing drain spacing; actual size ratio, smear and well resistance change together. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drainage-length scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：僅在相同無因次幾何與材料參數的擴散尺度比較，L₁=5 m、L₂=1 m，t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Only for diffusion scaling with identical dimensionless geometry and material parameters, L₁=5 m and L₂=1 m give t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04.","failure":"常見誤解：「排水距離減成五分之一，現場工期一定固定變成百分之四。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reducing drainage length to one fifth always makes the field duration exactly four percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「排水距離尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drainage-length scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-01-k1","title":"排水距離尺度的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification","text":"排水路徑縮短會加快壓力擴散，理想擴散時間隨特徵長度平方變化，這是垂直排水構想的基礎。實際排水板網格同時改變影響半徑、井徑比與塗抹比例，不能只用長度平方比直接預測現場工期；土層排水方向也需要辨識。","textEn":"Shorter drainage paths accelerate pressure diffusion, whose ideal characteristic time varies with squared length. This motivates vertical drains, but actual spacing changes influence radius, drain-size ratio and smear proportion together.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排水距離減成五分之一，現場工期一定固定變成百分之四。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reducing drainage length to one fifth always makes the field duration exactly four percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「排水距離尺度的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["排水距離減成五分之一，現場工期一定固定變成百分之四。","排水路徑縮短會加快壓力擴散，理想擴散時間隨特徵長度平方變化，這是垂直排水構想的基礎。","三角與方形網格可以無條件用相同的等效直徑係數。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing drainage length to one fifth always makes the field duration exactly four percent.","Shorter drainage paths accelerate pressure diffusion, whose ideal characteristic time varies with squared length.","Triangular and square grids can always use the same influence-diameter coefficient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"排水路徑縮短會加快壓力擴散，理想擴散時間隨特徵長度平方變化，這是垂直排水構想的基礎。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shorter drainage paths accelerate pressure diffusion, whose ideal characteristic time varies with squared length. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b190-v14-02","title":"排水距離尺度的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排水距離尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drainage-length scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：僅在相同無因次幾何與材料參數的擴散尺度比較，L₁=5 m、L₂=1 m，t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Only for diffusion scaling with identical dimensionless geometry and material parameters, L₁=5 m and L₂=1 m give t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以壓密試驗與分層孔壓建立排水方向，對照試驗區時間曲線，檢查塗抹與井阻是否主導。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use consolidation tests and multilevel pore pressure to define drainage direction, comparing trial-area time histories and checking whether smear or well resistance dominates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：僅在相同無因次幾何與材料參數的擴散尺度比較，L₁=5 m、L₂=1 m，t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Only for diffusion scaling with identical dimensionless geometry and material parameters, L₁=5 m and L₂=1 m give t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「排水距離尺度的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["徑向時間因子等於零點六三就代表完成百分之六十三。","水進入排水板後就沒有任何沿程水頭損失。","原創教學假設：僅在相同無因次幾何與材料參數的擴散尺度比較，L₁=5 m、L₂=1 m，t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04。"],"optionsEn":["A radial time factor of 0.63 means sixty-three-percent consolidation.","Water experiences no head loss after entering a vertical drain.","Original teaching assumptions: Only for diffusion scaling with identical dimensionless geometry and material parameters, L₁=5 m and L₂=1 m give t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：僅在相同無因次幾何與材料參數的擴散尺度比較，L₁=5 m、L₂=1 m，t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Only for diffusion scaling with identical dimensionless geometry and material parameters, L₁=5 m and L₂=1 m give t₂/t₁=(L₂/L₁)²=0.04. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b190-v14-03","title":"排水距離尺度的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水距離尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drainage-length scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以壓密試驗與分層孔壓建立排水方向，對照試驗區時間曲線，檢查塗抹與井阻是否主導。設計者應分開記錄尺度示意與實際徑向壓密模型；卸載須依觀測而非單一平方比例放行。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use consolidation tests and multilevel pore pressure to define drainage direction, comparing trial-area time histories and checking whether smear or well resistance dominates. The designer separates scaling illustration from actual radial-consolidation modelling; unloading follows observations rather than one squared ratio. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計者應分開記錄尺度示意與實際徑向壓密模型；卸載須依觀測而非單一平方比例放行。本比值特別保持無因次參數不變，並非排水板間距改變後的工期比；實際n、塗抹與井阻會一同變動。","observationEn":"Site practice: The designer separates scaling illustration from actual radial-consolidation modelling; unloading follows observations rather than one squared ratio. This ratio explicitly holds dimensionless parameters fixed and is not the schedule ratio after changing drain spacing; actual size ratio, smear and well resistance change together.","failure":"注意干擾：把理想百分之四時間當實際排程，會提前卸除預壓，留下未消散孔壓與後續沉陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using the ideal four-percent time as a schedule can release surcharge early, leaving excess pressure and later settlement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以壓密試驗與分層孔壓建立排水方向，對照試驗區時間曲線，檢查塗抹與井阻是否主導。設計者應分開記錄尺度示意與實際徑向壓密模型；卸載須依觀測而非單一平方比例放行。","textEn":"Use consolidation tests and multilevel pore pressure to define drainage direction, comparing trial-area time histories and checking whether smear or well resistance dominates. The designer separates scaling illustration from actual radial-consolidation modelling; unloading follows observations rather than one squared ratio.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計者應分開記錄尺度示意與實際徑向壓密模型；卸載須依觀測而非單一平方比例放行。本比值特別保持無因次參數不變，並非排水板間距改變後的工期比；實際n、塗抹與井阻會一同變動。","textEn":"The designer separates scaling illustration from actual radial-consolidation modelling; unloading follows observations rather than one squared ratio. This ratio explicitly holds dimensionless parameters fixed and is not the schedule ratio after changing drain spacing; actual size ratio, smear and well resistance change together.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「排水距離尺度的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以壓密試驗與分層孔壓建立排水方向，對照試驗區時間曲線，檢查塗抹與井阻是否主導。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","裝設排水板會把軟土的最終壓縮沉陷直接消除。"],"optionsEn":["Use consolidation tests and multilevel pore pressure to define drainage direction, comparing trial-area time histories and checking whether smear or well resistance dominates.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Installing vertical drains directly eliminates ultimate compressive settlement of soft soil."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以壓密試驗與分層孔壓建立排水方向，對照試驗區時間曲線，檢查塗抹與井阻是否主導。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use consolidation tests and multilevel pore pressure to define drainage direction, comparing trial-area time histories and checking whether smear or well resistance dominates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b190-v14-04","title":"排水距離尺度的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排水距離尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drainage-length scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把理想百分之四時間當實際排程，會提前卸除預壓，留下未消散孔壓與後續沉陷。本比值特別保持無因次參數不變，並非排水板間距改變後的工期比；實際n、塗抹與井阻會一同變動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using the ideal four-percent time as a schedule can release surcharge early, leaving excess pressure and later settlement. This ratio explicitly holds dimensionless parameters fixed and is not the schedule ratio after changing drain spacing; actual size ratio, smear and well resistance change together. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本比值特別保持無因次參數不變，並非排水板間距改變後的工期比；實際n、塗抹與井阻會一同變動。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This ratio explicitly holds dimensionless parameters fixed and is not the schedule ratio after changing drain spacing; actual size ratio, smear and well resistance change together.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排水距離減成五分之一，現場工期一定固定變成百分之四。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reducing drainage length to one fifth always makes the field duration exactly four percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把理想百分之四時間當實際排程，會提前卸除預壓，留下未消散孔壓與後續沉陷。本比值特別保持無因次參數不變，並非排水板間距改變後的工期比；實際n、塗抹與井阻會一同變動。","textEn":"Using the ideal four-percent time as a schedule can release surcharge early, leaving excess pressure and later settlement. This ratio explicitly holds dimensionless parameters fixed and is not the schedule ratio after changing drain spacing; actual size ratio, smear and well resistance change together.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「排水距離尺度的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drainage-length scale mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把理想百分之四時間當實際排程，會提前卸除預壓，留下未消散孔壓與後續沉陷。","三角與方形網格可以無條件用相同的等效直徑係數。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using the ideal four-percent time as a schedule can release surcharge early, leaving excess pressure and later settlement.","Triangular and square grids can always use the same influence-diameter coefficient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把理想百分之四時間當實際排程，會提前卸除預壓，留下未消散孔壓與後續沉陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using the ideal four-percent time as a schedule can release surcharge early, leaving excess pressure and later settlement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b190-v14-05","title":"三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「三角網格影響徑」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Triangular-grid influence diameter” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"排水板網格把土體分成單井影響單元，等效圓面積用於徑向壓密分析。三角形與方形排列有不同的面積換算，施工偏位及漏插又會形成較大未排水區；名目間距需要與實際安裝位置一起驗證。係數一點零五是等面積近似，不描述邊界單元或排水不均；異常網格應以實際幾何重新建立模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「三角網格影響徑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A drain grid divides soil into influence cells, represented by equivalent circular area in radial analysis. Triangular and square layouts use different area conversions, while misplaced or omitted drains create larger undrained zones. Nominal spacing therefore requires verification against actual installation positions rather than reliance on the layout drawing alone. The coefficient is an equal-area approximation, not a model of boundary cells or uneven drainage; irregular grids require revised geometry. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Triangular-grid influence diameter” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：三角形網格假設間距s=1.2 m，等效影響直徑de≈1.05s=1.26 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For a triangular grid with spacing s=1.2 m, equivalent influence diameter de≈1.05s=1.26 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「三角與方形網格可以無條件用相同的等效直徑係數。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Triangular and square grids can always use the same influence-diameter coefficient.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「三角網格影響徑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Triangular-grid influence diameter”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-05-k1","title":"三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification","text":"排水板網格把土體分成單井影響單元，等效圓面積用於徑向壓密分析。三角形與方形排列有不同的面積換算，施工偏位及漏插又會形成較大未排水區；名目間距需要與實際安裝位置一起驗證。","textEn":"A drain grid divides soil into influence cells, represented by equivalent circular area in radial analysis. Triangular and square layouts use different area conversions, while misplaced or omitted drains create larger undrained zones.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：三角與方形網格可以無條件用相同的等效直徑係數。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Triangular and square grids can always use the same influence-diameter coefficient. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["三角與方形網格可以無條件用相同的等效直徑係數。","等效直徑相同的排水板就一定有相同通水能力。","排水板網格把土體分成單井影響單元，等效圓面積用於徑向壓密分析。"],"optionsEn":["Triangular and square grids can always use the same influence-diameter coefficient.","Drains with the same equivalent diameter have identical discharge capacity.","A drain grid divides soil into influence cells, represented by equivalent circular area in radial analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"排水板網格把土體分成單井影響單元，等效圓面積用於徑向壓密分析。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A drain grid divides soil into influence cells, represented by equivalent circular area in radial analysis. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b190-v14-06","title":"三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「三角網格影響徑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Triangular-grid influence diameter” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：三角形網格假設間距s=1.2 m，等效影響直徑de≈1.05s=1.26 m。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For a triangular grid with spacing s=1.2 m, equivalent influence diameter de≈1.05s=1.26 m. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將實際插設座標與設計網格疊合，檢查邊界、障礙物及漏插區，計算最不利單元面積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Overlay actual installation coordinates on the design grid, checking boundaries, obstacles and omissions and calculating adverse influence-cell areas.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：三角形網格假設間距s=1.2 m，等效影響直徑de≈1.05s=1.26 m。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For a triangular grid with spacing s=1.2 m, equivalent influence diameter de≈1.05s=1.26 m. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：三角形網格假設間距s=1.2 m，等效影響直徑de≈1.05s=1.26 m。","插設擾動只影響施工方便，對長期排水速度沒有影響。","加上八十千帕預壓，就立刻增加八十千帕有效應力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For a triangular grid with spacing s=1.2 m, equivalent influence diameter de≈1.05s=1.26 m.","Installation disturbance affects convenience but not long-term drainage rate.","Applying eighty kilopascals of surcharge immediately adds the same effective stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：三角形網格假設間距s=1.2 m，等效影響直徑de≈1.05s=1.26 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For a triangular grid with spacing s=1.2 m, equivalent influence diameter de≈1.05s=1.26 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b190-v14-07","title":"三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「三角網格影響徑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Triangular-grid influence diameter” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將實際插設座標與設計網格疊合，檢查邊界、障礙物及漏插區，計算最不利單元面積。竣工網格須保留實際位置與未完成深度；地工設計者核定補插及監測點代表性後才驗收。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Overlay actual installation coordinates on the design grid, checking boundaries, obstacles and omissions and calculating adverse influence-cell areas. As-built grids retain actual positions and incomplete depths; the geotechnical designer approves additional drains and monitoring representativeness before acceptance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：竣工網格須保留實際位置與未完成深度；地工設計者核定補插及監測點代表性後才驗收。係數一點零五是等面積近似，不描述邊界單元或排水不均；異常網格應以實際幾何重新建立模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: As-built grids retain actual positions and incomplete depths; the geotechnical designer approves additional drains and monitoring representativeness before acceptance. The coefficient is an equal-area approximation, not a model of boundary cells or uneven drainage; irregular grids require revised geometry.","failure":"注意干擾：漏插或偏位可能留下排水盲區，周圍測點反應良好仍無法代表該局部壓密程度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omission or displacement leaves a drainage blind zone that favourable surrounding measurements do not represent. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將實際插設座標與設計網格疊合，檢查邊界、障礙物及漏插區，計算最不利單元面積。竣工網格須保留實際位置與未完成深度；地工設計者核定補插及監測點代表性後才驗收。","textEn":"Overlay actual installation coordinates on the design grid, checking boundaries, obstacles and omissions and calculating adverse influence-cell areas. As-built grids retain actual positions and incomplete depths; the geotechnical designer approves additional drains and monitoring representativeness before acceptance.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"竣工網格須保留實際位置與未完成深度；地工設計者核定補插及監測點代表性後才驗收。係數一點零五是等面積近似，不描述邊界單元或排水不均；異常網格應以實際幾何重新建立模型。","textEn":"As-built grids retain actual positions and incomplete depths; the geotechnical designer approves additional drains and monitoring representativeness before acceptance. The coefficient is an equal-area approximation, not a model of boundary cells or uneven drainage; irregular grids require revised geometry.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將實際插設座標與設計網格疊合，檢查邊界、障礙物及漏插區，計算最不利單元面積。","現場出水量減少就一定表示排水板已經堵塞。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Overlay actual installation coordinates on the design grid, checking boundaries, obstacles and omissions and calculating adverse influence-cell areas.","Reduced field discharge necessarily means the drain has clogged."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將實際插設座標與設計網格疊合，檢查邊界、障礙物及漏插區，計算最不利單元面積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Overlay actual installation coordinates on the design grid, checking boundaries, obstacles and omissions and calculating adverse influence-cell areas. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b190-v14-08","title":"三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「三角網格影響徑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Triangular-grid influence diameter” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏插或偏位可能留下排水盲區，周圍測點反應良好仍無法代表該局部壓密程度。係數一點零五是等面積近似，不描述邊界單元或排水不均；異常網格應以實際幾何重新建立模型。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omission or displacement leaves a drainage blind zone that favourable surrounding measurements do not represent. The coefficient is an equal-area approximation, not a model of boundary cells or uneven drainage; irregular grids require revised geometry. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：係數一點零五是等面積近似，不描述邊界單元或排水不均；異常網格應以實際幾何重新建立模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The coefficient is an equal-area approximation, not a model of boundary cells or uneven drainage; irregular grids require revised geometry.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「三角與方形網格可以無條件用相同的等效直徑係數。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Triangular and square grids can always use the same influence-diameter coefficient.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏插或偏位可能留下排水盲區，周圍測點反應良好仍無法代表該局部壓密程度。係數一點零五是等面積近似，不描述邊界單元或排水不均；異常網格應以實際幾何重新建立模型。","textEn":"Omission or displacement leaves a drainage blind zone that favourable surrounding measurements do not represent. The coefficient is an equal-area approximation, not a model of boundary cells or uneven drainage; irregular grids require revised geometry.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「三角網格影響徑的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Triangular-grid influence diameter mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","等效直徑相同的排水板就一定有相同通水能力。","漏插或偏位可能留下排水盲區，周圍測點反應良好仍無法代表該局部壓密程度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Drains with the same equivalent diameter have identical discharge capacity.","Omission or displacement leaves a drainage blind zone that favourable surrounding measurements do not represent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏插或偏位可能留下排水盲區，周圍測點反應良好仍無法代表該局部壓密程度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omission or displacement leaves a drainage blind zone that favourable surrounding measurements do not represent. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b190-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證」與「徑向時間因子的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification\" and \"Radial time factor mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b190-v14-09","title":"帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「帶狀排水板等效徑」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Equivalent band-drain diameter” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"排水板是帶狀而非圓管，徑向土體分析常以等效圓直徑表示其周長效果。寬度與厚度之外，濾布透水性、芯材通道及受壓後變形都影響排水，幾何等效不等於水力容量等效，也不能直接套用砂井直徑。等周長式屬模型近似，不是流道內徑；受壓排水能力及土體濾層相容性需要獨立的水力試驗。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「帶狀排水板等效徑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Band drains are not circular pipes, so radial soil analysis commonly uses an equivalent diameter related to perimeter. Width and thickness do not capture filter permeability, core channels or compression. Geometric equivalence therefore is not hydraulic-capacity equivalence and cannot be substituted directly for a sand-drain diameter. The perimeter relation is a modelling approximation, not internal channel diameter; confined discharge and soil-filter compatibility need separate hydraulic tests. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Equivalent band-drain diameter” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設帶寬b=0.10 m、厚t=0.004 m，等周長等效dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For width b=0.10 m and thickness t=0.004 m, perimeter-equivalent dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「等效直徑相同的排水板就一定有相同通水能力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Drains with the same equivalent diameter have identical discharge capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「帶狀排水板等效徑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Equivalent band-drain diameter”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-09-k1","title":"帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification","text":"排水板是帶狀而非圓管，徑向土體分析常以等效圓直徑表示其周長效果。寬度與厚度之外，濾布透水性、芯材通道及受壓後變形都影響排水，幾何等效不等於水力容量等效，也不能直接套用砂井直徑。","textEn":"Band drains are not circular pipes, so radial soil analysis commonly uses an equivalent diameter related to perimeter. Width and thickness do not capture filter permeability, core channels or compression.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：等效直徑相同的排水板就一定有相同通水能力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Drains with the same equivalent diameter have identical discharge capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["排水板是帶狀而非圓管，徑向土體分析常以等效圓直徑表示其周長效果。","等效直徑相同的排水板就一定有相同通水能力。","徑向時間因子等於零點六三就代表完成百分之六十三。"],"optionsEn":["Band drains are not circular pipes, so radial soil analysis commonly uses an equivalent diameter related to perimeter.","Drains with the same equivalent diameter have identical discharge capacity.","A radial time factor of 0.63 means sixty-three-percent consolidation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"排水板是帶狀而非圓管，徑向土體分析常以等效圓直徑表示其周長效果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Band drains are not circular pipes, so radial soil analysis commonly uses an equivalent diameter related to perimeter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b190-v14-10","title":"帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「帶狀排水板等效徑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Equivalent band-drain diameter” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設帶寬b=0.10 m、厚t=0.004 m，等周長等效dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For width b=0.10 m and thickness t=0.004 m, perimeter-equivalent dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對產品尺寸與受圍壓排水試驗，檢查彎折後通道及濾布狀態，分列等效直徑與通水量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify product dimensions and confined-flow tests, inspect channels and filter after bending, and report equivalent diameter separately from discharge capacity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設帶寬b=0.10 m、厚t=0.004 m，等周長等效dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For width b=0.10 m and thickness t=0.004 m, perimeter-equivalent dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["水進入排水板後就沒有任何沿程水頭損失。","原創教學假設：假設帶寬b=0.10 m、厚t=0.004 m，等周長等效dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m。","裝設排水板會把軟土的最終壓縮沉陷直接消除。"],"optionsEn":["Water experiences no head loss after entering a vertical drain.","Original teaching assumptions: For width b=0.10 m and thickness t=0.004 m, perimeter-equivalent dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m.","Installing vertical drains directly eliminates ultimate compressive settlement of soft soil."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設帶寬b=0.10 m、厚t=0.004 m，等周長等效dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For width b=0.10 m and thickness t=0.004 m, perimeter-equivalent dw=2(b+t)/π=0.0662 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b190-v14-11","title":"帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「帶狀排水板等效徑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Equivalent band-drain diameter” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對產品尺寸與受圍壓排水試驗，檢查彎折後通道及濾布狀態，分列等效直徑與通水量。材料驗收應核對受壓、彎折及濾布試驗條件；設計者確認與實際土壓及沉陷相符後才採用。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify product dimensions and confined-flow tests, inspect channels and filter after bending, and report equivalent diameter separately from discharge capacity. Acceptance checks confinement, bending and filter test conditions; the designer confirms their relevance to actual earth pressure and settlement before use. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：材料驗收應核對受壓、彎折及濾布試驗條件；設計者確認與實際土壓及沉陷相符後才採用。等周長式屬模型近似，不是流道內徑；受壓排水能力及土體濾層相容性需要獨立的水力試驗。","observationEn":"Site practice: Acceptance checks confinement, bending and filter test conditions; the designer confirms their relevance to actual earth pressure and settlement before use. The perimeter relation is a modelling approximation, not internal channel diameter; confined discharge and soil-filter compatibility need separate hydraulic tests.","failure":"注意干擾：只按等效直徑選材可能忽略芯材壓潰或濾布堵塞，實際井阻遠大於設計假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Selecting by equivalent diameter alone can miss crushed cores or clogged filters, producing much greater well resistance than assumed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對產品尺寸與受圍壓排水試驗，檢查彎折後通道及濾布狀態，分列等效直徑與通水量。材料驗收應核對受壓、彎折及濾布試驗條件；設計者確認與實際土壓及沉陷相符後才採用。","textEn":"Verify product dimensions and confined-flow tests, inspect channels and filter after bending, and report equivalent diameter separately from discharge capacity. Acceptance checks confinement, bending and filter test conditions; the designer confirms their relevance to actual earth pressure and settlement before use.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"材料驗收應核對受壓、彎折及濾布試驗條件；設計者確認與實際土壓及沉陷相符後才採用。等周長式屬模型近似，不是流道內徑；受壓排水能力及土體濾層相容性需要獨立的水力試驗。","textEn":"Acceptance checks confinement, bending and filter test conditions; the designer confirms their relevance to actual earth pressure and settlement before use. The perimeter relation is a modelling approximation, not internal channel diameter; confined discharge and soil-filter compatibility need separate hydraulic tests.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","地表沉陷看似停止就表示所有深度的孔壓都消散。","核對產品尺寸與受圍壓排水試驗，檢查彎折後通道及濾布狀態，分列等效直徑與通水量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Apparently stopped surface settlement proves pore pressure has dissipated at every depth.","Verify product dimensions and confined-flow tests, inspect channels and filter after bending, and report equivalent diameter separately from discharge capacity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對產品尺寸與受圍壓排水試驗，檢查彎折後通道及濾布狀態，分列等效直徑與通水量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify product dimensions and confined-flow tests, inspect channels and filter after bending, and report equivalent diameter separately from discharge capacity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b190-v14-12","title":"帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「帶狀排水板等效徑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Equivalent band-drain diameter” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只按等效直徑選材可能忽略芯材壓潰或濾布堵塞，實際井阻遠大於設計假設。等周長式屬模型近似，不是流道內徑；受壓排水能力及土體濾層相容性需要獨立的水力試驗。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Selecting by equivalent diameter alone can miss crushed cores or clogged filters, producing much greater well resistance than assumed. The perimeter relation is a modelling approximation, not internal channel diameter; confined discharge and soil-filter compatibility need separate hydraulic tests. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：等周長式屬模型近似，不是流道內徑；受壓排水能力及土體濾層相容性需要獨立的水力試驗。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The perimeter relation is a modelling approximation, not internal channel diameter; confined discharge and soil-filter compatibility need separate hydraulic tests.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「等效直徑相同的排水板就一定有相同通水能力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Drains with the same equivalent diameter have identical discharge capacity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只按等效直徑選材可能忽略芯材壓潰或濾布堵塞，實際井阻遠大於設計假設。等周長式屬模型近似，不是流道內徑；受壓排水能力及土體濾層相容性需要獨立的水力試驗。","textEn":"Selecting by equivalent diameter alone can miss crushed cores or clogged filters, producing much greater well resistance than assumed. The perimeter relation is a modelling approximation, not internal channel diameter; confined discharge and soil-filter compatibility need separate hydraulic tests.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「帶狀排水板等效徑的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equivalent band-drain diameter mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只按等效直徑選材可能忽略芯材壓潰或濾布堵塞，實際井阻遠大於設計假設。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","徑向時間因子等於零點六三就代表完成百分之六十三。"],"optionsEn":["Selecting by equivalent diameter alone can miss crushed cores or clogged filters, producing much greater well resistance than assumed.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A radial time factor of 0.63 means sixty-three-percent consolidation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只按等效直徑選材可能忽略芯材壓潰或濾布堵塞，實際井阻遠大於設計假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Selecting by equivalent diameter alone can miss crushed cores or clogged filters, producing much greater well resistance than assumed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b190-v14-13","title":"徑向時間因子的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Radial time factor mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「徑向時間因子」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Radial time factor” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"徑向壓密的時間因子把水平壓密係數、時間及單井影響尺寸結合，便於比較不同觀測時段。它本身不是壓密完成度，還需井徑比、塗抹與井阻的函數；水平係數也不能無條件用垂直壓密試驗值替代。本算例明確使用平方公尺每一天，時間亦以天計；要從Tr求壓密度，還必須指定所採理論及全部無因次參數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「徑向時間因子」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The radial time factor combines horizontal consolidation coefficient, time and cell size to compare observation periods. It is not itself degree of consolidation, which also depends on drain-size ratio, smear and well resistance. Horizontal coefficients cannot automatically be replaced by vertical-test values without justification of anisotropy. This example explicitly uses square metres per day and time in days; converting Tr to consolidation degree still requires the selected theory and all dimensionless parameters. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Radial time factor” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設ch=0.01 m²/day、t=100 day、de=1.26 m，Tr=ch t/de²=0.630，無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For ch=0.01 m²/day, t=100 day and de=1.26 m, Tr=ch t/de²=0.630, dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「徑向時間因子等於零點六三就代表完成百分之六十三。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A radial time factor of 0.63 means sixty-three-percent consolidation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「徑向時間因子」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Radial time factor”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-13-k1","title":"徑向時間因子的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Radial time factor mechanism and verification","text":"徑向壓密的時間因子把水平壓密係數、時間及單井影響尺寸結合，便於比較不同觀測時段。它本身不是壓密完成度，還需井徑比、塗抹與井阻的函數；水平係數也不能無條件用垂直壓密試驗值替代。","textEn":"The radial time factor combines horizontal consolidation coefficient, time and cell size to compare observation periods. It is not itself degree of consolidation, which also depends on drain-size ratio, smear and well resistance.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：徑向時間因子等於零點六三就代表完成百分之六十三。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A radial time factor of 0.63 means sixty-three-percent consolidation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「徑向時間因子的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Radial time factor mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["徑向時間因子等於零點六三就代表完成百分之六十三。","徑向壓密的時間因子把水平壓密係數、時間及單井影響尺寸結合，便於比較不同觀測時段。","插設擾動只影響施工方便，對長期排水速度沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["A radial time factor of 0.63 means sixty-three-percent consolidation.","The radial time factor combines horizontal consolidation coefficient, time and cell size to compare observation periods.","Installation disturbance affects convenience but not long-term drainage rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"徑向壓密的時間因子把水平壓密係數、時間及單井影響尺寸結合，便於比較不同觀測時段。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The radial time factor combines horizontal consolidation coefficient, time and cell size to compare observation periods. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b190-v14-14","title":"徑向時間因子的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Radial time factor mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「徑向時間因子」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Radial time factor” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設ch=0.01 m²/day、t=100 day、de=1.26 m，Tr=ch t/de²=0.630，無因次。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For ch=0.01 m²/day, t=100 day and de=1.26 m, Tr=ch t/de²=0.630, dimensionless. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以試驗區孔壓及沉陷曲線反算ch範圍，保留獨立測點驗證，確認時間單位與係數完全一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Back-analyse a range of ch from trial-area pressure and settlement, retain independent validation points, and verify consistent time units in all coefficients.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設ch=0.01 m²/day、t=100 day、de=1.26 m，Tr=ch t/de²=0.630，無因次。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For ch=0.01 m²/day, t=100 day and de=1.26 m, Tr=ch t/de²=0.630, dimensionless. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「徑向時間因子的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Radial time factor mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["加上八十千帕預壓，就立刻增加八十千帕有效應力。","現場出水量減少就一定表示排水板已經堵塞。","原創教學假設：假設ch=0.01 m²/day、t=100 day、de=1.26 m，Tr=ch t/de²=0.630，無因次。"],"optionsEn":["Applying eighty kilopascals of surcharge immediately adds the same effective stress.","Reduced field discharge necessarily means the drain has clogged.","Original teaching assumptions: For ch=0.01 m²/day, t=100 day and de=1.26 m, Tr=ch t/de²=0.630, dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設ch=0.01 m²/day、t=100 day、de=1.26 m，Tr=ch t/de²=0.630，無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For ch=0.01 m²/day, t=100 day and de=1.26 m, Tr=ch t/de²=0.630, dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b190-v14-15","title":"徑向時間因子的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Radial time factor mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「徑向時間因子」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Radial time factor” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以試驗區孔壓及沉陷曲線反算ch範圍，保留獨立測點驗證，確認時間單位與係數完全一致。計算書須標示ch的試驗方向、單位與應力範圍；地工設計者核准完整壓密函數後再作排程推估。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Back-analyse a range of ch from trial-area pressure and settlement, retain independent validation points, and verify consistent time units in all coefficients. State ch direction, units and stress range; the geotechnical designer approves the full consolidation function before schedule estimation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：計算書須標示ch的試驗方向、單位與應力範圍；地工設計者核准完整壓密函數後再作排程推估。本算例明確使用平方公尺每一天，時間亦以天計；要從Tr求壓密度，還必須指定所採理論及全部無因次參數。","observationEn":"Site practice: State ch direction, units and stress range; the geotechnical designer approves the full consolidation function before schedule estimation. This example explicitly uses square metres per day and time in days; converting Tr to consolidation degree still requires the selected theory and all dimensionless parameters.","failure":"注意干擾：把日與秒混用會造成巨大工期誤差，把Tr當完成率則會在機制尚未確認時提前卸載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing days and seconds creates major schedule errors, while treating Tr as completion percentage can release surcharge before the mechanism is verified. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以試驗區孔壓及沉陷曲線反算ch範圍，保留獨立測點驗證，確認時間單位與係數完全一致。計算書須標示ch的試驗方向、單位與應力範圍；地工設計者核准完整壓密函數後再作排程推估。","textEn":"Back-analyse a range of ch from trial-area pressure and settlement, retain independent validation points, and verify consistent time units in all coefficients. State ch direction, units and stress range; the geotechnical designer approves the full consolidation function before schedule estimation.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"計算書須標示ch的試驗方向、單位與應力範圍；地工設計者核准完整壓密函數後再作排程推估。本算例明確使用平方公尺每一天，時間亦以天計；要從Tr求壓密度，還必須指定所採理論及全部無因次參數。","textEn":"State ch direction, units and stress range; the geotechnical designer approves the full consolidation function before schedule estimation. This example explicitly uses square metres per day and time in days; converting Tr to consolidation degree still requires the selected theory and all dimensionless parameters.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「徑向時間因子的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Radial time factor mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以試驗區孔壓及沉陷曲線反算ch範圍，保留獨立測點驗證，確認時間單位與係數完全一致。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","排水距離減成五分之一，現場工期一定固定變成百分之四。"],"optionsEn":["Back-analyse a range of ch from trial-area pressure and settlement, retain independent validation points, and verify consistent time units in all coefficients.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Reducing drainage length to one fifth always makes the field duration exactly four percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以試驗區孔壓及沉陷曲線反算ch範圍，保留獨立測點驗證，確認時間單位與係數完全一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Back-analyse a range of ch from trial-area pressure and settlement, retain independent validation points, and verify consistent time units in all coefficients. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b190-v14-16","title":"徑向時間因子的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Radial time factor mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「徑向時間因子」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Radial time factor” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把日與秒混用會造成巨大工期誤差，把Tr當完成率則會在機制尚未確認時提前卸載。本算例明確使用平方公尺每一天，時間亦以天計；要從Tr求壓密度，還必須指定所採理論及全部無因次參數。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing days and seconds creates major schedule errors, while treating Tr as completion percentage can release surcharge before the mechanism is verified. This example explicitly uses square metres per day and time in days; converting Tr to consolidation degree still requires the selected theory and all dimensionless parameters. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本算例明確使用平方公尺每一天，時間亦以天計；要從Tr求壓密度，還必須指定所採理論及全部無因次參數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This example explicitly uses square metres per day and time in days; converting Tr to consolidation degree still requires the selected theory and all dimensionless parameters.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「徑向時間因子等於零點六三就代表完成百分之六十三。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A radial time factor of 0.63 means sixty-three-percent consolidation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把日與秒混用會造成巨大工期誤差，把Tr當完成率則會在機制尚未確認時提前卸載。本算例明確使用平方公尺每一天，時間亦以天計；要從Tr求壓密度，還必須指定所採理論及全部無因次參數。","textEn":"Mixing days and seconds creates major schedule errors, while treating Tr as completion percentage can release surcharge before the mechanism is verified. This example explicitly uses square metres per day and time in days; converting Tr to consolidation degree still requires the selected theory and all dimensionless parameters.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「徑向時間因子的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Radial time factor mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把日與秒混用會造成巨大工期誤差，把Tr當完成率則會在機制尚未確認時提前卸載。","插設擾動只影響施工方便，對長期排水速度沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Mixing days and seconds creates major schedule errors, while treating Tr as completion percentage can release surcharge before the mechanism is verified.","Installation disturbance affects convenience but not long-term drainage rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把日與秒混用會造成巨大工期誤差，把Tr當完成率則會在機制尚未確認時提前卸載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing days and seconds creates major schedule errors, while treating Tr as completion percentage can release surcharge before the mechanism is verified. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b190-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證」與「排水井阻的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification\" and \"Well resistance mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b190-v14-17","title":"塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「塗抹區滲透性」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Smear-zone permeability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"插設套管擾動排水板周圍土體，可能重塑黏土並形成低水平滲透性的塗抹區。排水路徑雖變短，水仍需穿越這個局部阻力；因此增加排水板數量不一定按理想比例加速壓密，工具尺寸與土體敏感性需共同考慮。滲透比不足以完整描述塗抹效應，還需要塗抹區尺寸與原土各向異性；不能把本比值當普遍材料常數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「塗抹區滲透性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Installation mandrels disturb surrounding soil, potentially remoulding clay into a zone of lower horizontal permeability. Although the drainage path shortens, water must still cross this local resistance. More drains therefore need not accelerate consolidation by the ideal proportion, and tool size and soil sensitivity must be considered together. Permeability ratio alone does not define smear; its extent and native-soil anisotropy are also needed, and this ratio is not universal. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Smear-zone permeability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設塗抹區ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、未擾動kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s，比值ks/kh=0.20。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For smear permeability ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s and undisturbed kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s, ks/kh=0.20.","failure":"常見誤解：「插設擾動只影響施工方便，對長期排水速度沒有影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Installation disturbance affects convenience but not long-term drainage rate.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「塗抹區滲透性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Smear-zone permeability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-17-k1","title":"塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification","text":"插設套管擾動排水板周圍土體，可能重塑黏土並形成低水平滲透性的塗抹區。排水路徑雖變短，水仍需穿越這個局部阻力；因此增加排水板數量不一定按理想比例加速壓密，工具尺寸與土體敏感性需共同考慮。","textEn":"Installation mandrels disturb surrounding soil, potentially remoulding clay into a zone of lower horizontal permeability. Although the drainage path shortens, water must still cross this local resistance.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：插設擾動只影響施工方便，對長期排水速度沒有影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Installation disturbance affects convenience but not long-term drainage rate. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["插設擾動只影響施工方便，對長期排水速度沒有影響。","水進入排水板後就沒有任何沿程水頭損失。","插設套管擾動排水板周圍土體，可能重塑黏土並形成低水平滲透性的塗抹區。"],"optionsEn":["Installation disturbance affects convenience but not long-term drainage rate.","Water experiences no head loss after entering a vertical drain.","Installation mandrels disturb surrounding soil, potentially remoulding clay into a zone of lower horizontal permeability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"插設套管擾動排水板周圍土體，可能重塑黏土並形成低水平滲透性的塗抹區。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Installation mandrels disturb surrounding soil, potentially remoulding clay into a zone of lower horizontal permeability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b190-v14-18","title":"塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塗抹區滲透性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Smear-zone permeability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設塗抹區ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、未擾動kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s，比值ks/kh=0.20。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For smear permeability ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s and undisturbed kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s, ks/kh=0.20. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較靠近及遠離排水板的孔壓消散，核對套管尺寸與土體重塑試驗，辨識塗抹半徑和滲透性的不確定度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare dissipation near and away from drains, verify mandrel dimensions and remoulding tests, and assess uncertainty in smear radius and permeability.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設塗抹區ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、未擾動kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s，比值ks/kh=0.20。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For smear permeability ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s and undisturbed kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s, ks/kh=0.20. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：假設塗抹區ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、未擾動kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s，比值ks/kh=0.20。","裝設排水板會把軟土的最終壓縮沉陷直接消除。","地表沉陷看似停止就表示所有深度的孔壓都消散。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For smear permeability ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s and undisturbed kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s, ks/kh=0.20.","Installing vertical drains directly eliminates ultimate compressive settlement of soft soil.","Apparently stopped surface settlement proves pore pressure has dissipated at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設塗抹區ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s、未擾動kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s，比值ks/kh=0.20。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For smear permeability ks=1×10⁻⁹ m/s and undisturbed kh=5×10⁻⁹ m/s, ks/kh=0.20. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b190-v14-19","title":"塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塗抹區滲透性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Smear-zone permeability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較靠近及遠離排水板的孔壓消散，核對套管尺寸與土體重塑試驗，辨識塗抹半徑和滲透性的不確定度。安裝設備與套管尺寸變更需重審塗抹假設；地工設計者以試驗區反應核定實際設計參數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare dissipation near and away from drains, verify mandrel dimensions and remoulding tests, and assess uncertainty in smear radius and permeability. Changing installation equipment or mandrel size requires review of smear assumptions; the geotechnical designer approves parameters using trial-area response. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：安裝設備與套管尺寸變更需重審塗抹假設；地工設計者以試驗區反應核定實際設計參數。滲透比不足以完整描述塗抹效應，還需要塗抹區尺寸與原土各向異性；不能把本比值當普遍材料常數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Changing installation equipment or mandrel size requires review of smear assumptions; the geotechnical designer approves parameters using trial-area response. Permeability ratio alone does not define smear; its extent and native-soil anisotropy are also needed, and this ratio is not universal.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略塗抹會高估排水速率，試驗區尚未達預期便需重新解釋模型，而非只增加預壓荷重。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring smear overpredicts drainage rate; underperforming trials require model reassessment rather than merely adding surcharge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較靠近及遠離排水板的孔壓消散，核對套管尺寸與土體重塑試驗，辨識塗抹半徑和滲透性的不確定度。安裝設備與套管尺寸變更需重審塗抹假設；地工設計者以試驗區反應核定實際設計參數。","textEn":"Compare dissipation near and away from drains, verify mandrel dimensions and remoulding tests, and assess uncertainty in smear radius and permeability. Changing installation equipment or mandrel size requires review of smear assumptions; the geotechnical designer approves parameters using trial-area response.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"安裝設備與套管尺寸變更需重審塗抹假設；地工設計者以試驗區反應核定實際設計參數。滲透比不足以完整描述塗抹效應，還需要塗抹區尺寸與原土各向異性；不能把本比值當普遍材料常數。","textEn":"Changing installation equipment or mandrel size requires review of smear assumptions; the geotechnical designer approves parameters using trial-area response. Permeability ratio alone does not define smear; its extent and native-soil anisotropy are also needed, and this ratio is not universal.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","比較靠近及遠離排水板的孔壓消散，核對套管尺寸與土體重塑試驗，辨識塗抹半徑和滲透性的不確定度。","三角與方形網格可以無條件用相同的等效直徑係數。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare dissipation near and away from drains, verify mandrel dimensions and remoulding tests, and assess uncertainty in smear radius and permeability.","Triangular and square grids can always use the same influence-diameter coefficient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較靠近及遠離排水板的孔壓消散，核對套管尺寸與土體重塑試驗，辨識塗抹半徑和滲透性的不確定度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare dissipation near and away from drains, verify mandrel dimensions and remoulding tests, and assess uncertainty in smear radius and permeability. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b190-v14-20","title":"塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塗抹區滲透性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Smear-zone permeability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略塗抹會高估排水速率，試驗區尚未達預期便需重新解釋模型，而非只增加預壓荷重。滲透比不足以完整描述塗抹效應，還需要塗抹區尺寸與原土各向異性；不能把本比值當普遍材料常數。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring smear overpredicts drainage rate; underperforming trials require model reassessment rather than merely adding surcharge. Permeability ratio alone does not define smear; its extent and native-soil anisotropy are also needed, and this ratio is not universal. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：滲透比不足以完整描述塗抹效應，還需要塗抹區尺寸與原土各向異性；不能把本比值當普遍材料常數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Permeability ratio alone does not define smear; its extent and native-soil anisotropy are also needed, and this ratio is not universal.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「插設擾動只影響施工方便，對長期排水速度沒有影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Installation disturbance affects convenience but not long-term drainage rate.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略塗抹會高估排水速率，試驗區尚未達預期便需重新解釋模型，而非只增加預壓荷重。滲透比不足以完整描述塗抹效應，還需要塗抹區尺寸與原土各向異性；不能把本比值當普遍材料常數。","textEn":"Ignoring smear overpredicts drainage rate; underperforming trials require model reassessment rather than merely adding surcharge. Permeability ratio alone does not define smear; its extent and native-soil anisotropy are also needed, and this ratio is not universal.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「塗抹區滲透性的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Smear-zone permeability mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","水進入排水板後就沒有任何沿程水頭損失。","忽略塗抹會高估排水速率，試驗區尚未達預期便需重新解釋模型，而非只增加預壓荷重。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Water experiences no head loss after entering a vertical drain.","Ignoring smear overpredicts drainage rate; underperforming trials require model reassessment rather than merely adding surcharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略塗抹會高估排水速率，試驗區尚未達預期便需重新解釋模型，而非只增加預壓荷重。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring smear overpredicts drainage rate; underperforming trials require model reassessment rather than merely adding surcharge. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b190-v14-21","title":"排水井阻的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Well resistance mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「排水井阻」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Well resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水進入排水板後還必須沿芯材向排水層流動，長排水板、圍壓及彎折可能造成顯著井阻。把排水板當成零水頭損失邊界會高估深部排水，砂墊層及出口不暢也可能限制整個系統，需分辨土內阻力與排水通道阻力。這是指定工況的等效阻力而非材料常數，與長度、圍壓及流量條件有關；井阻模型需保留實際排水方向。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水井阻」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After entering the drain, water travels along the core to an outlet. Long drains, confinement and bending can create significant well resistance. Assuming zero drain head loss overestimates deep drainage, while a restricted blanket or outlet can govern the whole system. Distinguish soil resistance from resistance inside the drainage path. This is equivalent resistance for one condition, not a material constant; length, confinement and flow matter, and the well-resistance model must retain the actual drainage direction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Well resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設水頭損失Δh=2 m、流量Q=0.0001 m³/s，等效水力阻力R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For head loss Δh=2 m and discharge Q=0.0001 m³/s, hydraulic resistance R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m².","failure":"常見誤解：「水進入排水板後就沒有任何沿程水頭損失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Water experiences no head loss after entering a vertical drain.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「排水井阻」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Well resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-21-k1","title":"排水井阻的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Well resistance mechanism and verification","text":"水進入排水板後還必須沿芯材向排水層流動，長排水板、圍壓及彎折可能造成顯著井阻。把排水板當成零水頭損失邊界會高估深部排水，砂墊層及出口不暢也可能限制整個系統，需分辨土內阻力與排水通道阻力。","textEn":"After entering the drain, water travels along the core to an outlet. Long drains, confinement and bending can create significant well resistance.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水進入排水板後就沒有任何沿程水頭損失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Water experiences no head loss after entering a vertical drain. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「排水井阻的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Well resistance mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["水進入排水板後還必須沿芯材向排水層流動，長排水板、圍壓及彎折可能造成顯著井阻。","水進入排水板後就沒有任何沿程水頭損失。","加上八十千帕預壓，就立刻增加八十千帕有效應力。"],"optionsEn":["After entering the drain, water travels along the core to an outlet.","Water experiences no head loss after entering a vertical drain.","Applying eighty kilopascals of surcharge immediately adds the same effective stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水進入排水板後還必須沿芯材向排水層流動，長排水板、圍壓及彎折可能造成顯著井阻。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After entering the drain, water travels along the core to an outlet. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b190-v14-22","title":"排水井阻的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Well resistance mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排水井阻」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Well resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設水頭損失Δh=2 m、流量Q=0.0001 m³/s，等效水力阻力R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m²。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For head loss Δh=2 m and discharge Q=0.0001 m³/s, hydraulic resistance R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m². This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測排水通道上不同高程水頭並核對出水量，將受壓通水試驗與現場彎折及沉陷條件比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure heads at different elevations along the drainage path and outlet flow, comparing confined discharge tests with field bending and settlement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設水頭損失Δh=2 m、流量Q=0.0001 m³/s，等效水力阻力R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m²。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For head loss Δh=2 m and discharge Q=0.0001 m³/s, hydraulic resistance R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m². This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「排水井阻的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Well resistance mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["現場出水量減少就一定表示排水板已經堵塞。","原創教學假設：假設水頭損失Δh=2 m、流量Q=0.0001 m³/s，等效水力阻力R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m²。","排水距離減成五分之一，現場工期一定固定變成百分之四。"],"optionsEn":["Reduced field discharge necessarily means the drain has clogged.","Original teaching assumptions: For head loss Δh=2 m and discharge Q=0.0001 m³/s, hydraulic resistance R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m².","Reducing drainage length to one fifth always makes the field duration exactly four percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設水頭損失Δh=2 m、流量Q=0.0001 m³/s，等效水力阻力R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For head loss Δh=2 m and discharge Q=0.0001 m³/s, hydraulic resistance R=Δh/Q=20000 s/m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b190-v14-23","title":"排水井阻的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Well resistance mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水井阻」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Well resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測排水通道上不同高程水頭並核對出水量，將受壓通水試驗與現場彎折及沉陷條件比較。交接須含排水墊層與出口通達性；地工及排水設計者確認整條流路後才接受排水系統。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure heads at different elevations along the drainage path and outlet flow, comparing confined discharge tests with field bending and settlement. Handover includes drainage blankets and outlet access; geotechnical and drainage designers confirm the entire path before accepting the system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接須含排水墊層與出口通達性；地工及排水設計者確認整條流路後才接受排水系統。這是指定工況的等效阻力而非材料常數，與長度、圍壓及流量條件有關；井阻模型需保留實際排水方向。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover includes drainage blankets and outlet access; geotechnical and drainage designers confirm the entire path before accepting the system. This is equivalent resistance for one condition, not a material constant; length, confinement and flow matter, and the well-resistance model must retain the actual drainage direction.","failure":"注意干擾：出口堵塞或芯材壓縮會讓深部孔壓消散落後，表層沉陷較快也不能證明全深有效排水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A blocked outlet or compressed core delays deep pressure dissipation, and rapid shallow settlement does not prove effective full-depth drainage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測排水通道上不同高程水頭並核對出水量，將受壓通水試驗與現場彎折及沉陷條件比較。交接須含排水墊層與出口通達性；地工及排水設計者確認整條流路後才接受排水系統。","textEn":"Measure heads at different elevations along the drainage path and outlet flow, comparing confined discharge tests with field bending and settlement. Handover includes drainage blankets and outlet access; geotechnical and drainage designers confirm the entire path before accepting the system.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接須含排水墊層與出口通達性；地工及排水設計者確認整條流路後才接受排水系統。這是指定工況的等效阻力而非材料常數，與長度、圍壓及流量條件有關；井阻模型需保留實際排水方向。","textEn":"Handover includes drainage blankets and outlet access; geotechnical and drainage designers confirm the entire path before accepting the system. This is equivalent resistance for one condition, not a material constant; length, confinement and flow matter, and the well-resistance model must retain the actual drainage direction.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「排水井阻的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Well resistance mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","等效直徑相同的排水板就一定有相同通水能力。","量測排水通道上不同高程水頭並核對出水量，將受壓通水試驗與現場彎折及沉陷條件比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Drains with the same equivalent diameter have identical discharge capacity.","Measure heads at different elevations along the drainage path and outlet flow, comparing confined discharge tests with field bending and settlement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測排水通道上不同高程水頭並核對出水量，將受壓通水試驗與現場彎折及沉陷條件比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure heads at different elevations along the drainage path and outlet flow, comparing confined discharge tests with field bending and settlement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b190-v14-24","title":"排水井阻的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Well resistance mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排水井阻」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Well resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出口堵塞或芯材壓縮會讓深部孔壓消散落後，表層沉陷較快也不能證明全深有效排水。這是指定工況的等效阻力而非材料常數，與長度、圍壓及流量條件有關；井阻模型需保留實際排水方向。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A blocked outlet or compressed core delays deep pressure dissipation, and rapid shallow settlement does not prove effective full-depth drainage. This is equivalent resistance for one condition, not a material constant; length, confinement and flow matter, and the well-resistance model must retain the actual drainage direction. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這是指定工況的等效阻力而非材料常數，與長度、圍壓及流量條件有關；井阻模型需保留實際排水方向。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This is equivalent resistance for one condition, not a material constant; length, confinement and flow matter, and the well-resistance model must retain the actual drainage direction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水進入排水板後就沒有任何沿程水頭損失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Water experiences no head loss after entering a vertical drain.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出口堵塞或芯材壓縮會讓深部孔壓消散落後，表層沉陷較快也不能證明全深有效排水。這是指定工況的等效阻力而非材料常數，與長度、圍壓及流量條件有關；井阻模型需保留實際排水方向。","textEn":"A blocked outlet or compressed core delays deep pressure dissipation, and rapid shallow settlement does not prove effective full-depth drainage. This is equivalent resistance for one condition, not a material constant; length, confinement and flow matter, and the well-resistance model must retain the actual drainage direction.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「排水井阻的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Well resistance mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["出口堵塞或芯材壓縮會讓深部孔壓消散落後，表層沉陷較快也不能證明全深有效排水。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","加上八十千帕預壓，就立刻增加八十千帕有效應力。"],"optionsEn":["A blocked outlet or compressed core delays deep pressure dissipation, and rapid shallow settlement does not prove effective full-depth drainage.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Applying eighty kilopascals of surcharge immediately adds the same effective stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"出口堵塞或芯材壓縮會讓深部孔壓消散落後，表層沉陷較快也不能證明全深有效排水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A blocked outlet or compressed core delays deep pressure dissipation, and rapid shallow settlement does not prove effective full-depth drainage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b190-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「有效應力成長的機理與驗證」與「對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification\" and \"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b190-v14-25","title":"有效應力成長的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「有效應力成長」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective-stress gain” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"預壓荷載初期可主要轉成超額孔壓，隨排水消散，更多荷載才移交給土骨架並引起壓密。若只量測地表荷重而沒有孔壓，就不能判定有效應力增加多少；水位變化與不同土層的初始壓力也需用同一基準處理。增量式需同一位置與時刻且正負號一致，不能把絕對孔壓混入超額孔壓；總應力分布還受荷載擴散影響。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效應力成長」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Surcharge may initially appear mainly as excess pore pressure; drainage progressively transfers more load to the skeleton and causes consolidation. Applied surface load alone cannot establish effective-stress gain without pressure observations. Groundwater changes and layer-specific initial pressures also require one consistent reference. The increment relation requires the same location, time and sign convention; absolute and excess pressures are not interchangeable, and total stress also reflects load spread. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective-stress gain” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設總應力增量Δσ=80 kPa、殘餘超額孔壓Δu=30 kPa，Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For total-stress increment Δσ=80 kPa and remaining excess pressure Δu=30 kPa, effective increment Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「加上八十千帕預壓，就立刻增加八十千帕有效應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Applying eighty kilopascals of surcharge immediately adds the same effective stress.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效應力成長」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective-stress gain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-25-k1","title":"有效應力成長的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification","text":"預壓荷載初期可主要轉成超額孔壓，隨排水消散，更多荷載才移交給土骨架並引起壓密。若只量測地表荷重而沒有孔壓，就不能判定有效應力增加多少；水位變化與不同土層的初始壓力也需用同一基準處理。","textEn":"Surcharge may initially appear mainly as excess pore pressure; drainage progressively transfers more load to the skeleton and causes consolidation. Applied surface load alone cannot establish effective-stress gain without pressure observations.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：加上八十千帕預壓，就立刻增加八十千帕有效應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Applying eighty kilopascals of surcharge immediately adds the same effective stress. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「有效應力成長的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["加上八十千帕預壓，就立刻增加八十千帕有效應力。","預壓荷載初期可主要轉成超額孔壓，隨排水消散，更多荷載才移交給土骨架並引起壓密。","裝設排水板會把軟土的最終壓縮沉陷直接消除。"],"optionsEn":["Applying eighty kilopascals of surcharge immediately adds the same effective stress.","Surcharge may initially appear mainly as excess pore pressure; drainage progressively transfers more load to the skeleton and causes consolidation.","Installing vertical drains directly eliminates ultimate compressive settlement of soft soil."],"answer":1,"explanation":"預壓荷載初期可主要轉成超額孔壓，隨排水消散，更多荷載才移交給土骨架並引起壓密。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Surcharge may initially appear mainly as excess pore pressure; drainage progressively transfers more load to the skeleton and causes consolidation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b190-v14-26","title":"有效應力成長的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效應力成長」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective-stress gain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設總應力增量Δσ=80 kPa、殘餘超額孔壓Δu=30 kPa，Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For total-stress increment Δσ=80 kPa and remaining excess pressure Δu=30 kPa, effective increment Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多深度孔壓與預壓高程核對荷載歷程，確認儀器基準水壓及地下水位變化，分層求有效增量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use multilevel pore pressure and surcharge elevation to reconstruct load history, checking baseline pressure and groundwater changes before calculating layer-wise effective increments.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設總應力增量Δσ=80 kPa、殘餘超額孔壓Δu=30 kPa，Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For total-stress increment Δσ=80 kPa and remaining excess pressure Δu=30 kPa, effective increment Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「有效應力成長的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["地表沉陷看似停止就表示所有深度的孔壓都消散。","三角與方形網格可以無條件用相同的等效直徑係數。","原創教學假設：假設總應力增量Δσ=80 kPa、殘餘超額孔壓Δu=30 kPa，Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa。"],"optionsEn":["Apparently stopped surface settlement proves pore pressure has dissipated at every depth.","Triangular and square grids can always use the same influence-diameter coefficient.","Original teaching assumptions: For total-stress increment Δσ=80 kPa and remaining excess pressure Δu=30 kPa, effective increment Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設總應力增量Δσ=80 kPa、殘餘超額孔壓Δu=30 kPa，Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For total-stress increment Δσ=80 kPa and remaining excess pressure Δu=30 kPa, effective increment Δσ′=Δσ−Δu=50 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b190-v14-27","title":"有效應力成長的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效應力成長」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective-stress gain” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多深度孔壓與預壓高程核對荷載歷程，確認儀器基準水壓及地下水位變化，分層求有效增量。每階段荷載與孔壓應同步歸檔；地工設計者確認有效應力及穩定需求後才核准加載或卸載。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use multilevel pore pressure and surcharge elevation to reconstruct load history, checking baseline pressure and groundwater changes before calculating layer-wise effective increments. Archive each loading stage with synchronized pore pressures; the geotechnical designer confirms effective stress and stability requirements before loading or unloading. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：每階段荷載與孔壓應同步歸檔；地工設計者確認有效應力及穩定需求後才核准加載或卸載。增量式需同一位置與時刻且正負號一致，不能把絕對孔壓混入超額孔壓；總應力分布還受荷載擴散影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Archive each loading stage with synchronized pore pressures; the geotechnical designer confirms effective stress and stability requirements before loading or unloading. The increment relation requires the same location, time and sign convention; absolute and excess pressures are not interchangeable, and total stress also reflects load spread.","failure":"注意干擾：把預壓全重當成已完成有效應力，會高估土體強度及壓密度，卸載後留下可觀後續沉陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating all surcharge as mobilized effective stress overstates strength and consolidation and can leave substantial later settlement after unloading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多深度孔壓與預壓高程核對荷載歷程，確認儀器基準水壓及地下水位變化，分層求有效增量。每階段荷載與孔壓應同步歸檔；地工設計者確認有效應力及穩定需求後才核准加載或卸載。","textEn":"Use multilevel pore pressure and surcharge elevation to reconstruct load history, checking baseline pressure and groundwater changes before calculating layer-wise effective increments. Archive each loading stage with synchronized pore pressures; the geotechnical designer confirms effective stress and stability requirements before loading or unloading.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"每階段荷載與孔壓應同步歸檔；地工設計者確認有效應力及穩定需求後才核准加載或卸載。增量式需同一位置與時刻且正負號一致，不能把絕對孔壓混入超額孔壓；總應力分布還受荷載擴散影響。","textEn":"Archive each loading stage with synchronized pore pressures; the geotechnical designer confirms effective stress and stability requirements before loading or unloading. The increment relation requires the same location, time and sign convention; absolute and excess pressures are not interchangeable, and total stress also reflects load spread.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「有效應力成長的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以多深度孔壓與預壓高程核對荷載歷程，確認儀器基準水壓及地下水位變化，分層求有效增量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","徑向時間因子等於零點六三就代表完成百分之六十三。"],"optionsEn":["Use multilevel pore pressure and surcharge elevation to reconstruct load history, checking baseline pressure and groundwater changes before calculating layer-wise effective increments.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A radial time factor of 0.63 means sixty-three-percent consolidation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以多深度孔壓與預壓高程核對荷載歷程，確認儀器基準水壓及地下水位變化，分層求有效增量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use multilevel pore pressure and surcharge elevation to reconstruct load history, checking baseline pressure and groundwater changes before calculating layer-wise effective increments. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b190-v14-28","title":"有效應力成長的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效應力成長」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective-stress gain” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把預壓全重當成已完成有效應力，會高估土體強度及壓密度，卸載後留下可觀後續沉陷。增量式需同一位置與時刻且正負號一致，不能把絕對孔壓混入超額孔壓；總應力分布還受荷載擴散影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating all surcharge as mobilized effective stress overstates strength and consolidation and can leave substantial later settlement after unloading. The increment relation requires the same location, time and sign convention; absolute and excess pressures are not interchangeable, and total stress also reflects load spread. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：增量式需同一位置與時刻且正負號一致，不能把絕對孔壓混入超額孔壓；總應力分布還受荷載擴散影響。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The increment relation requires the same location, time and sign convention; absolute and excess pressures are not interchangeable, and total stress also reflects load spread.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「加上八十千帕預壓，就立刻增加八十千帕有效應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Applying eighty kilopascals of surcharge immediately adds the same effective stress.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把預壓全重當成已完成有效應力，會高估土體強度及壓密度，卸載後留下可觀後續沉陷。增量式需同一位置與時刻且正負號一致，不能把絕對孔壓混入超額孔壓；總應力分布還受荷載擴散影響。","textEn":"Treating all surcharge as mobilized effective stress overstates strength and consolidation and can leave substantial later settlement after unloading. The increment relation requires the same location, time and sign convention; absolute and excess pressures are not interchangeable, and total stress also reflects load spread.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「有效應力成長的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective-stress gain mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把預壓全重當成已完成有效應力，會高估土體強度及壓密度，卸載後留下可觀後續沉陷。","裝設排水板會把軟土的最終壓縮沉陷直接消除。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating all surcharge as mobilized effective stress overstates strength and consolidation and can leave substantial later settlement after unloading.","Installing vertical drains directly eliminates ultimate compressive settlement of soft soil."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把預壓全重當成已完成有效應力，會高估土體強度及壓密度，卸載後留下可觀後續沉陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating all surcharge as mobilized effective stress overstates strength and consolidation and can leave substantial later settlement after unloading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b190-v14-29","title":"對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「對數壓縮沉陷」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Logarithmic compression settlement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"正常壓密黏土在一維條件下可用壓縮指數與有效應力對數關係估算沉陷，排水板主要改變到達此沉陷的速度而非終值。若存在先期壓密、不同應力路徑或次壓密，需分段採用相應參數，不能把一條正常壓密線套用所有土層。此式明定正常壓密、一維及以十為底對數，未含側移；Cc為無因次斜率，不能與以自然對數定義的參數混用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「對數壓縮沉陷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For normally consolidated clay in one-dimensional conditions, compression index and logarithmic effective stress estimate settlement. Drains mainly change how quickly settlement occurs rather than its ultimate value. Preconsolidation, different stress paths and secondary compression require appropriate segments and parameters instead of one virgin-compression line for every layer. The formula specifies normally consolidated one-dimensional behaviour and base-ten logarithms, excluding lateral movement; dimensionless Cc cannot be mixed with a natural-log parameter. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Logarithmic compression settlement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設Cc=0.3、H=10 m、e₀=1.0、σ′₀=100 kPa、σ′f=150 kPa，s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For Cc=0.3, H=10 m, e₀=1.0, σ′₀=100 kPa and σ′f=150 kPa, s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「裝設排水板會把軟土的最終壓縮沉陷直接消除。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Installing vertical drains directly eliminates ultimate compressive settlement of soft soil.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「對數壓縮沉陷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Logarithmic compression settlement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-29-k1","title":"對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification","text":"正常壓密黏土在一維條件下可用壓縮指數與有效應力對數關係估算沉陷，排水板主要改變到達此沉陷的速度而非終值。若存在先期壓密、不同應力路徑或次壓密，需分段採用相應參數，不能把一條正常壓密線套用所有土層。","textEn":"For normally consolidated clay in one-dimensional conditions, compression index and logarithmic effective stress estimate settlement. Drains mainly change how quickly settlement occurs rather than its ultimate value.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裝設排水板會把軟土的最終壓縮沉陷直接消除。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Installing vertical drains directly eliminates ultimate compressive settlement of soft soil. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["裝設排水板會把軟土的最終壓縮沉陷直接消除。","現場出水量減少就一定表示排水板已經堵塞。","正常壓密黏土在一維條件下可用壓縮指數與有效應力對數關係估算沉陷，排水板主要改變到達此沉陷的速度而非終值。"],"optionsEn":["Installing vertical drains directly eliminates ultimate compressive settlement of soft soil.","Reduced field discharge necessarily means the drain has clogged.","For normally consolidated clay in one-dimensional conditions, compression index and logarithmic effective stress estimate settlement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"正常壓密黏土在一維條件下可用壓縮指數與有效應力對數關係估算沉陷，排水板主要改變到達此沉陷的速度而非終值。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For normally consolidated clay in one-dimensional conditions, compression index and logarithmic effective stress estimate settlement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b190-v14-30","title":"對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「對數壓縮沉陷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Logarithmic compression settlement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設Cc=0.3、H=10 m、e₀=1.0、σ′₀=100 kPa、σ′f=150 kPa，s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For Cc=0.3, H=10 m, e₀=1.0, σ′₀=100 kPa and σ′f=150 kPa, s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以壓密試驗核對先期壓密壓力與指數，使用分層沉陷計比較，確認應力增量及厚度代表性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check preconsolidation pressure and indices from consolidation tests, compare layered settlement, and verify representative stress increments and thicknesses.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設Cc=0.3、H=10 m、e₀=1.0、σ′₀=100 kPa、σ′f=150 kPa，s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For Cc=0.3, H=10 m, e₀=1.0, σ′₀=100 kPa and σ′f=150 kPa, s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：假設Cc=0.3、H=10 m、e₀=1.0、σ′₀=100 kPa、σ′f=150 kPa，s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m。","排水距離減成五分之一，現場工期一定固定變成百分之四。","等效直徑相同的排水板就一定有相同通水能力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: For Cc=0.3, H=10 m, e₀=1.0, σ′₀=100 kPa and σ′f=150 kPa, s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m.","Reducing drainage length to one fifth always makes the field duration exactly four percent.","Drains with the same equivalent diameter have identical discharge capacity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設Cc=0.3、H=10 m、e₀=1.0、σ′₀=100 kPa、σ′f=150 kPa，s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For Cc=0.3, H=10 m, e₀=1.0, σ′₀=100 kPa and σ′f=150 kPa, s=CcH/(1+e₀) log₁₀(σ′f/σ′₀)=0.264 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b190-v14-31","title":"對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「對數壓縮沉陷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Logarithmic compression settlement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以壓密試驗核對先期壓密壓力與指數，使用分層沉陷計比較，確認應力增量及厚度代表性。設計與交接應分開主要壓密及長期次壓密預測；地工設計者確認參數適用應力範圍後再解讀監測。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check preconsolidation pressure and indices from consolidation tests, compare layered settlement, and verify representative stress increments and thicknesses. Separate primary and secondary settlement in design and handover; the geotechnical designer confirms parameter stress ranges before interpreting monitoring. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計與交接應分開主要壓密及長期次壓密預測；地工設計者確認參數適用應力範圍後再解讀監測。此式明定正常壓密、一維及以十為底對數，未含側移；Cc為無因次斜率，不能與以自然對數定義的參數混用。","observationEn":"Site practice: Separate primary and secondary settlement in design and handover; the geotechnical designer confirms parameter stress ranges before interpreting monitoring. The formula specifies normally consolidated one-dimensional behaviour and base-ten logarithms, excluding lateral movement; dimensionless Cc cannot be mixed with a natural-log parameter.","failure":"注意干擾：誤把超壓密土全程用正常壓密指數，可能高估或錯估沉陷；忽略次壓密則會漏掉長期變形。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying virgin compression throughout an overconsolidated path mispredicts settlement, while neglecting secondary compression misses long-term movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以壓密試驗核對先期壓密壓力與指數，使用分層沉陷計比較，確認應力增量及厚度代表性。設計與交接應分開主要壓密及長期次壓密預測；地工設計者確認參數適用應力範圍後再解讀監測。","textEn":"Check preconsolidation pressure and indices from consolidation tests, compare layered settlement, and verify representative stress increments and thicknesses. Separate primary and secondary settlement in design and handover; the geotechnical designer confirms parameter stress ranges before interpreting monitoring.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計與交接應分開主要壓密及長期次壓密預測；地工設計者確認參數適用應力範圍後再解讀監測。此式明定正常壓密、一維及以十為底對數，未含側移；Cc為無因次斜率，不能與以自然對數定義的參數混用。","textEn":"Separate primary and secondary settlement in design and handover; the geotechnical designer confirms parameter stress ranges before interpreting monitoring. The formula specifies normally consolidated one-dimensional behaviour and base-ten logarithms, excluding lateral movement; dimensionless Cc cannot be mixed with a natural-log parameter.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以壓密試驗核對先期壓密壓力與指數，使用分層沉陷計比較，確認應力增量及厚度代表性。","插設擾動只影響施工方便，對長期排水速度沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Check preconsolidation pressure and indices from consolidation tests, compare layered settlement, and verify representative stress increments and thicknesses.","Installation disturbance affects convenience but not long-term drainage rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以壓密試驗核對先期壓密壓力與指數，使用分層沉陷計比較，確認應力增量及厚度代表性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check preconsolidation pressure and indices from consolidation tests, compare layered settlement, and verify representative stress increments and thicknesses. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b190-v14-32","title":"對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「對數壓縮沉陷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Logarithmic compression settlement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"誤把超壓密土全程用正常壓密指數，可能高估或錯估沉陷；忽略次壓密則會漏掉長期變形。此式明定正常壓密、一維及以十為底對數，未含側移；Cc為無因次斜率，不能與以自然對數定義的參數混用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying virgin compression throughout an overconsolidated path mispredicts settlement, while neglecting secondary compression misses long-term movement. The formula specifies normally consolidated one-dimensional behaviour and base-ten logarithms, excluding lateral movement; dimensionless Cc cannot be mixed with a natural-log parameter. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此式明定正常壓密、一維及以十為底對數，未含側移；Cc為無因次斜率，不能與以自然對數定義的參數混用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The formula specifies normally consolidated one-dimensional behaviour and base-ten logarithms, excluding lateral movement; dimensionless Cc cannot be mixed with a natural-log parameter.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裝設排水板會把軟土的最終壓縮沉陷直接消除。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Installing vertical drains directly eliminates ultimate compressive settlement of soft soil.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"誤把超壓密土全程用正常壓密指數，可能高估或錯估沉陷；忽略次壓密則會漏掉長期變形。此式明定正常壓密、一維及以十為底對數，未含側移；Cc為無因次斜率，不能與以自然對數定義的參數混用。","textEn":"Applying virgin compression throughout an overconsolidated path mispredicts settlement, while neglecting secondary compression misses long-term movement. The formula specifies normally consolidated one-dimensional behaviour and base-ten logarithms, excluding lateral movement; dimensionless Cc cannot be mixed with a natural-log parameter.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「對數壓縮沉陷的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Logarithmic compression settlement mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","現場出水量減少就一定表示排水板已經堵塞。","誤把超壓密土全程用正常壓密指數，可能高估或錯估沉陷；忽略次壓密則會漏掉長期變形。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Reduced field discharge necessarily means the drain has clogged.","Applying virgin compression throughout an overconsolidated path mispredicts settlement, while neglecting secondary compression misses long-term movement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"誤把超壓密土全程用正常壓密指數，可能高估或錯估沉陷；忽略次壓密則會漏掉長期變形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying virgin compression throughout an overconsolidated path mispredicts settlement, while neglecting secondary compression misses long-term movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b190-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「排水能力衰減的機理與驗證」與「壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification\" and \"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b190-v14-33","title":"排水能力衰減的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「排水能力衰減」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Discharge-capacity deterioration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"排水板隨土體沉陷彎折、圍壓增加或濾布堵塞，通水能力可能下降，因此出廠直條試驗不足以代表全工期。衰減比例應在相同水力坡降與圍壓下比較，才能辨別材料性能改變；現場出水下降也可能單純因超額孔壓已減少。百分比只對相同試驗邊界成立，不能把不同水頭下的流量直接比較；通水衰減也不等於壓密速度同比下降。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水能力衰減」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Drain bending during settlement, rising confinement and filter clogging can reduce discharge, so a straight factory test does not represent the whole project. Compare deterioration at consistent gradient and confinement to identify material change. Falling field discharge may instead reflect reduced excess pressure and must not automatically be called clogging. The percentage requires identical test boundaries; flow at different heads is not directly comparable, and capacity loss does not imply proportional slowing of consolidation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Discharge-capacity deterioration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：在相同試驗條件下，通水量Q₀=100 L/h降至Q₁=70 L/h，衰減(Q₀−Q₁)/Q₀=30%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Under identical test conditions, discharge falls from Q₀=100 L/h to Q₁=70 L/h, giving deterioration of 30%.","failure":"常見誤解：「現場出水量減少就一定表示排水板已經堵塞。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reduced field discharge necessarily means the drain has clogged.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「排水能力衰減」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Discharge-capacity deterioration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-33-k1","title":"排水能力衰減的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification","text":"排水板隨土體沉陷彎折、圍壓增加或濾布堵塞，通水能力可能下降，因此出廠直條試驗不足以代表全工期。衰減比例應在相同水力坡降與圍壓下比較，才能辨別材料性能改變；現場出水下降也可能單純因超額孔壓已減少。","textEn":"Drain bending during settlement, rising confinement and filter clogging can reduce discharge, so a straight factory test does not represent the whole project. Compare deterioration at consistent gradient and confinement to identify material change.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：現場出水量減少就一定表示排水板已經堵塞。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reduced field discharge necessarily means the drain has clogged. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「排水能力衰減的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["排水板隨土體沉陷彎折、圍壓增加或濾布堵塞，通水能力可能下降，因此出廠直條試驗不足以代表全工期。","現場出水量減少就一定表示排水板已經堵塞。","地表沉陷看似停止就表示所有深度的孔壓都消散。"],"optionsEn":["Drain bending during settlement, rising confinement and filter clogging can reduce discharge, so a straight factory test does not represent the whole project.","Reduced field discharge necessarily means the drain has clogged.","Apparently stopped surface settlement proves pore pressure has dissipated at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"排水板隨土體沉陷彎折、圍壓增加或濾布堵塞，通水能力可能下降，因此出廠直條試驗不足以代表全工期。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Drain bending during settlement, rising confinement and filter clogging can reduce discharge, so a straight factory test does not represent the whole project. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b190-v14-34","title":"排水能力衰減的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排水能力衰減」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Discharge-capacity deterioration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：在相同試驗條件下，通水量Q₀=100 L/h降至Q₁=70 L/h，衰減(Q₀−Q₁)/Q₀=30%。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Under identical test conditions, discharge falls from Q₀=100 L/h to Q₁=70 L/h, giving deterioration of 30%. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以受壓彎折試驗比較前後通水量，現場則同步看孔壓與排水量，區分能力下降及驅動水頭減少。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare confined bent-drain discharge before and after conditioning; in the field assess pressure and flow together to distinguish capacity loss from reduced driving head.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：在相同試驗條件下，通水量Q₀=100 L/h降至Q₁=70 L/h，衰減(Q₀−Q₁)/Q₀=30%。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Under identical test conditions, discharge falls from Q₀=100 L/h to Q₁=70 L/h, giving deterioration of 30%. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「排水能力衰減的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["三角與方形網格可以無條件用相同的等效直徑係數。","原創教學假設：在相同試驗條件下，通水量Q₀=100 L/h降至Q₁=70 L/h，衰減(Q₀−Q₁)/Q₀=30%。","徑向時間因子等於零點六三就代表完成百分之六十三。"],"optionsEn":["Triangular and square grids can always use the same influence-diameter coefficient.","Original teaching assumptions: Under identical test conditions, discharge falls from Q₀=100 L/h to Q₁=70 L/h, giving deterioration of 30%.","A radial time factor of 0.63 means sixty-three-percent consolidation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：在相同試驗條件下，通水量Q₀=100 L/h降至Q₁=70 L/h，衰減(Q₀−Q₁)/Q₀=30%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Under identical test conditions, discharge falls from Q₀=100 L/h to Q₁=70 L/h, giving deterioration of 30%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b190-v14-35","title":"排水能力衰減的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水能力衰減」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Discharge-capacity deterioration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以受壓彎折試驗比較前後通水量，現場則同步看孔壓與排水量，區分能力下降及驅動水頭減少。材料試驗需涵蓋預期圍壓與變形；地工設計者核定能力折減，營運端保留出口維護與監測責任。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare confined bent-drain discharge before and after conditioning; in the field assess pressure and flow together to distinguish capacity loss from reduced driving head. Material tests cover anticipated confinement and deformation; the geotechnical designer approves capacity reduction while operators retain outlet-maintenance and monitoring responsibility. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：材料試驗需涵蓋預期圍壓與變形；地工設計者核定能力折減，營運端保留出口維護與監測責任。百分比只對相同試驗邊界成立，不能把不同水頭下的流量直接比較；通水衰減也不等於壓密速度同比下降。","observationEn":"Site practice: Material tests cover anticipated confinement and deformation; the geotechnical designer approves capacity reduction while operators retain outlet-maintenance and monitoring responsibility. The percentage requires identical test boundaries; flow at different heads is not directly comparable, and capacity loss does not imply proportional slowing of consolidation.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略彎折與堵塞會讓深部排水變慢，若只按初始材料性能安排卸載，就可能留下殘餘孔壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring bending and clogging slows deep drainage; unloading based only on initial material performance can leave residual pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以受壓彎折試驗比較前後通水量，現場則同步看孔壓與排水量，區分能力下降及驅動水頭減少。材料試驗需涵蓋預期圍壓與變形；地工設計者核定能力折減，營運端保留出口維護與監測責任。","textEn":"Compare confined bent-drain discharge before and after conditioning; in the field assess pressure and flow together to distinguish capacity loss from reduced driving head. Material tests cover anticipated confinement and deformation; the geotechnical designer approves capacity reduction while operators retain outlet-maintenance and monitoring responsibility.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"材料試驗需涵蓋預期圍壓與變形；地工設計者核定能力折減，營運端保留出口維護與監測責任。百分比只對相同試驗邊界成立，不能把不同水頭下的流量直接比較；通水衰減也不等於壓密速度同比下降。","textEn":"Material tests cover anticipated confinement and deformation; the geotechnical designer approves capacity reduction while operators retain outlet-maintenance and monitoring responsibility. The percentage requires identical test boundaries; flow at different heads is not directly comparable, and capacity loss does not imply proportional slowing of consolidation.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「排水能力衰減的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","水進入排水板後就沒有任何沿程水頭損失。","以受壓彎折試驗比較前後通水量，現場則同步看孔壓與排水量，區分能力下降及驅動水頭減少。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Water experiences no head loss after entering a vertical drain.","Compare confined bent-drain discharge before and after conditioning."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以受壓彎折試驗比較前後通水量，現場則同步看孔壓與排水量，區分能力下降及驅動水頭減少。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare confined bent-drain discharge before and after conditioning; in the field assess pressure and flow together to distinguish capacity loss from reduced driving head. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b190-v14-36","title":"排水能力衰減的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排水能力衰減」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Discharge-capacity deterioration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略彎折與堵塞會讓深部排水變慢，若只按初始材料性能安排卸載，就可能留下殘餘孔壓。百分比只對相同試驗邊界成立，不能把不同水頭下的流量直接比較；通水衰減也不等於壓密速度同比下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring bending and clogging slows deep drainage; unloading based only on initial material performance can leave residual pressure. The percentage requires identical test boundaries; flow at different heads is not directly comparable, and capacity loss does not imply proportional slowing of consolidation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：百分比只對相同試驗邊界成立，不能把不同水頭下的流量直接比較；通水衰減也不等於壓密速度同比下降。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The percentage requires identical test boundaries; flow at different heads is not directly comparable, and capacity loss does not imply proportional slowing of consolidation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「現場出水量減少就一定表示排水板已經堵塞。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reduced field discharge necessarily means the drain has clogged.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略彎折與堵塞會讓深部排水變慢，若只按初始材料性能安排卸載，就可能留下殘餘孔壓。百分比只對相同試驗邊界成立，不能把不同水頭下的流量直接比較；通水衰減也不等於壓密速度同比下降。","textEn":"Ignoring bending and clogging slows deep drainage; unloading based only on initial material performance can leave residual pressure. The percentage requires identical test boundaries; flow at different heads is not directly comparable, and capacity loss does not imply proportional slowing of consolidation.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「排水能力衰減的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Discharge-capacity deterioration mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略彎折與堵塞會讓深部排水變慢，若只按初始材料性能安排卸載，就可能留下殘餘孔壓。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","地表沉陷看似停止就表示所有深度的孔壓都消散。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring bending and clogging slows deep drainage; unloading based only on initial material performance can leave residual pressure.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Apparently stopped surface settlement proves pore pressure has dissipated at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略彎折與堵塞會讓深部排水變慢，若只按初始材料性能安排卸載，就可能留下殘餘孔壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring bending and clogging slows deep drainage; unloading based only on initial material performance can leave residual pressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b190-v14-37","title":"壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「壓密度與卸載」如何影響砂井與垂直排水板的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Consolidation and unloading” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sand drains and prefabricated vertical drains”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"由實測沉陷除以估計最終主要壓密沉陷，可得到沉陷定義的平均壓密度，但分母本身有模型不確定度。地表沉陷可能混入側移或次壓密，孔壓定義的完成度也未必一致；卸載必須用多種證據確認剩餘變形符合資產需求。此壓密度以可靠的主要壓密終值為前提，不是通用卸載門檻；若終值重估，比例及殘餘沉陷都必須一起更新。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓密度與卸載」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Measured settlement divided by estimated ultimate primary settlement gives a settlement-based average consolidation degree, but its denominator is uncertain. Surface settlement may include lateral movement or secondary compression, and a pressure-based degree need not match exactly. Unloading therefore requires multiple evidence streams that confirm tolerable residual movement. This degree assumes a reliable ultimate primary settlement and is not a universal unloading threshold; revised ultimate estimates require updating both the ratio and residual settlement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Consolidation and unloading” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：假設已發生主要壓密沉陷s=240 mm、估計終值s∞=300 mm，Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: For measured primary settlement s=240 mm and estimated ultimate s∞=300 mm, Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%.","failure":"常見誤解：「地表沉陷看似停止就表示所有深度的孔壓都消散。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Apparently stopped surface settlement proves pore pressure has dissipated at every depth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓密度與卸載」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Consolidation and unloading”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-37-k1","title":"壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證","titleEn":"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification","text":"由實測沉陷除以估計最終主要壓密沉陷，可得到沉陷定義的平均壓密度，但分母本身有模型不確定度。地表沉陷可能混入側移或次壓密，孔壓定義的完成度也未必一致；卸載必須用多種證據確認剩餘變形符合資產需求。","textEn":"Measured settlement divided by estimated ultimate primary settlement gives a settlement-based average consolidation degree, but its denominator is uncertain. Surface settlement may include lateral movement or secondary compression, and a pressure-based degree need not match exactly.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地表沉陷看似停止就表示所有深度的孔壓都消散。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Apparently stopped surface settlement proves pore pressure has dissipated at every depth. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["地表沉陷看似停止就表示所有深度的孔壓都消散。","由實測沉陷除以估計最終主要壓密沉陷，可得到沉陷定義的平均壓密度，但分母本身有模型不確定度。","排水距離減成五分之一，現場工期一定固定變成百分之四。"],"optionsEn":["Apparently stopped surface settlement proves pore pressure has dissipated at every depth.","Measured settlement divided by estimated ultimate primary settlement gives a settlement-based average consolidation degree, but its denominator is uncertain.","Reducing drainage length to one fifth always makes the field duration exactly four percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"由實測沉陷除以估計最終主要壓密沉陷，可得到沉陷定義的平均壓密度，但分母本身有模型不確定度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Measured settlement divided by estimated ultimate primary settlement gives a settlement-based average consolidation degree, but its denominator is uncertain. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b190-v14-38","title":"壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓密度與卸載」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Consolidation and unloading” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：假設已發生主要壓密沉陷s=240 mm、估計終值s∞=300 mm，Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: For measured primary settlement s=240 mm and estimated ultimate s∞=300 mm, Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較沉陷外推與多深度孔壓消散，檢查最終沉陷估算對資料時窗的敏感度，保留未達標層位。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare settlement extrapolation with multilevel pressure dissipation, test sensitivity of ultimate-settlement estimates to the data window, and retain unresolved layers explicitly.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：假設已發生主要壓密沉陷s=240 mm、估計終值s∞=300 mm，Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%。此式用於量級與單位檢查，並非現場允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For measured primary settlement s=240 mm and estimated ultimate s∞=300 mm, Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%. This calculation checks scale and units; it is not a site acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["等效直徑相同的排水板就一定有相同通水能力。","插設擾動只影響施工方便，對長期排水速度沒有影響。","原創教學假設：假設已發生主要壓密沉陷s=240 mm、估計終值s∞=300 mm，Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%。"],"optionsEn":["Drains with the same equivalent diameter have identical discharge capacity.","Installation disturbance affects convenience but not long-term drainage rate.","Original teaching assumptions: For measured primary settlement s=240 mm and estimated ultimate s∞=300 mm, Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：假設已發生主要壓密沉陷s=240 mm、估計終值s∞=300 mm，Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: For measured primary settlement s=240 mm and estimated ultimate s∞=300 mm, Us=s/s∞=0.80=80%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b190-v14-39","title":"壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓密度與卸載」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Consolidation and unloading” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較沉陷外推與多深度孔壓消散，檢查最終沉陷估算對資料時窗的敏感度，保留未達標層位。卸載移交應由地工設計者及資產管理者共同核准，列明剩餘沉陷、回彈及長期監測條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare settlement extrapolation with multilevel pressure dissipation, test sensitivity of ultimate-settlement estimates to the data window, and retain unresolved layers explicitly. The geotechnical designer and asset owner jointly approve unloading and handover, documenting residual settlement, rebound and long-term monitoring conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：卸載移交應由地工設計者及資產管理者共同核准，列明剩餘沉陷、回彈及長期監測條件。此壓密度以可靠的主要壓密終值為前提，不是通用卸載門檻；若終值重估，比例及殘餘沉陷都必須一起更新。","observationEn":"Site practice: The geotechnical designer and asset owner jointly approve unloading and handover, documenting residual settlement, rebound and long-term monitoring conditions. This degree assumes a reliable ultimate primary settlement and is not a universal unloading threshold; revised ultimate estimates require updating both the ratio and residual settlement.","failure":"注意干擾：高估已完成比例會提前移除預壓，營運載重後再產生沉陷；只用地表平均可能漏掉深部未壓密層。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Overstating completion releases surcharge early and permits later settlement; surface averages can miss deep unconsolidated layers. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較沉陷外推與多深度孔壓消散，檢查最終沉陷估算對資料時窗的敏感度，保留未達標層位。卸載移交應由地工設計者及資產管理者共同核准，列明剩餘沉陷、回彈及長期監測條件。","textEn":"Compare settlement extrapolation with multilevel pressure dissipation, test sensitivity of ultimate-settlement estimates to the data window, and retain unresolved layers explicitly. The geotechnical designer and asset owner jointly approve unloading and handover, documenting residual settlement, rebound and long-term monitoring conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"卸載移交應由地工設計者及資產管理者共同核准，列明剩餘沉陷、回彈及長期監測條件。此壓密度以可靠的主要壓密終值為前提，不是通用卸載門檻；若終值重估，比例及殘餘沉陷都必須一起更新。","textEn":"The geotechnical designer and asset owner jointly approve unloading and handover, documenting residual settlement, rebound and long-term monitoring conditions. This degree assumes a reliable ultimate primary settlement and is not a universal unloading threshold; revised ultimate estimates require updating both the ratio and residual settlement.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification\"?","options":["比較沉陷外推與多深度孔壓消散，檢查最終沉陷估算對資料時窗的敏感度，保留未達標層位。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","加上八十千帕預壓，就立刻增加八十千帕有效應力。"],"optionsEn":["Compare settlement extrapolation with multilevel pressure dissipation, test sensitivity of ultimate-settlement estimates to the data window, and retain unresolved layers explicitly.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Applying eighty kilopascals of surcharge immediately adds the same effective stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較沉陷外推與多深度孔壓消散，檢查最終沉陷估算對資料時窗的敏感度，保留未達標層位。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare settlement extrapolation with multilevel pressure dissipation, test sensitivity of ultimate-settlement estimates to the data window, and retain unresolved layers explicitly. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b190-v14-40","title":"壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b190-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓密度與卸載」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Consolidation and unloading” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高估已完成比例會提前移除預壓，營運載重後再產生沉陷；只用地表平均可能漏掉深部未壓密層。此壓密度以可靠的主要壓密終值為前提，不是通用卸載門檻；若終值重估，比例及殘餘沉陷都必須一起更新。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Overstating completion releases surcharge early and permits later settlement; surface averages can miss deep unconsolidated layers. This degree assumes a reliable ultimate primary settlement and is not a universal unloading threshold; revised ultimate estimates require updating both the ratio and residual settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此壓密度以可靠的主要壓密終值為前提，不是通用卸載門檻；若終值重估，比例及殘餘沉陷都必須一起更新。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This degree assumes a reliable ultimate primary settlement and is not a universal unloading threshold; revised ultimate estimates require updating both the ratio and residual settlement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地表沉陷看似停止就表示所有深度的孔壓都消散。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Apparently stopped surface settlement proves pore pressure has dissipated at every depth.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b190-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高估已完成比例會提前移除預壓，營運載重後再產生沉陷；只用地表平均可能漏掉深部未壓密層。此壓密度以可靠的主要壓密終值為前提，不是通用卸載門檻；若終值重估，比例及殘餘沉陷都必須一起更新。","textEn":"Overstating completion releases surcharge early and permits later settlement; surface averages can miss deep unconsolidated layers. This degree assumes a reliable ultimate primary settlement and is not a universal unloading threshold; revised ultimate estimates require updating both the ratio and residual settlement.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]},{"id":"b190-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓密度與卸載的機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Consolidation and unloading mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","高估已完成比例會提前移除預壓，營運載重後再產生沉陷；只用地表平均可能漏掉深部未壓密層。","排水距離減成五分之一，現場工期一定固定變成百分之四。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Overstating completion releases surcharge early and permits later settlement; surface averages can miss deep unconsolidated layers.","Reducing drainage length to one fifth always makes the field duration exactly four percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高估已完成比例會提前移除預壓，營運載重後再產生沉陷；只用地表平均可能漏掉深部未壓密層。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Overstating completion releases surcharge early and permits later settlement; surface averages can miss deep unconsolidated layers. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-keller-drains","b-src-geotech","v14s-geo"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
